        "original_id": "8ae58183-68be-5ad7-92d3-b170ce1a985c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Charbonneau, Oregon\n- People: Jean Baptiste Charbonneau, Sacagawea\n- Topics: naming, languages, European travel\n\nFacts:\n- From 1823 to 1829, Jean Baptiste Charbonneau spent six years in Europe.\n- During his 1823 to 1829 time in Europe, Jean Baptiste Charbonneau learned German and Spanish.\n- Jean Baptiste Charbonneau spoke French and English.\n- Jean Baptiste Charbonneau was the son of Sacagawea.\n- The development of Charbonneau, Oregon, was named for Jean Baptiste Charbonneau.",
